.TH CW "1" "October 2026" "cw 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cw \- cw go
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cw
\fI\,go \/\fR[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,TARGET\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
Jump to a window (bring it to front).
.IP
TARGET can be a Context name, Context/Window, ref number, iTerm window
title, or "\-" to jump back.
.IP
Examples:
.TP
cw go MyProject
last used window in Context
.TP
cw go MyProject/Development
specific window by CW name
.TP
cw go \-
jump back to previous Context
.TP
cw go 3
window by ref number
.TP
cw go IoT
window by iTerm title
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this message and exit.
